Z||000007||Gokart||09-12-2000||10:13 PM||||The Fiero had been sitting for 3 to 4 years when I bought it and sat another year by the side of my house so you can imagine how much rust was on the chassis making it no good for anything but car heaven <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I just hope all the rodents that were living in it got hauled away too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000008||007DOUG||09-13-2000||12:14 AM||||Here's my 86 GT sitting at the Fiero factory in AL just before I picked it up.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttopbefore.jpg"> <P>I took them a stripped down frame. They installed T-tops and a 3.4<P>And one year later, its still sitting in my garage like that. The fiero is lowered 1", sway bars added, and KONI's at all four corners. The fastback GT body is already painted Audi pearl white, and the Mr Mike's interior is waiting to be installed.<P>I test-drove the car as you see it here. It was the first work I ever had completed by Ed Parks. I wanted to see if his workmanship was what everyone said it was. He put me a seat in, and I went flying up the road. He thought I was crazy. It was scarry, but fun!<P>(sigh) Some day I'll get time to put the body back on. It was a long summer without it.<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000009||gtsonly||09-14-2000||07:02 AM||||Naked Fiero's!!!!   Yahhhhhhhhhh Baby!!<BR>  Do I make you Horny? Do I make you Randie?<P>------------------<BR>Chris Hatch <BR>1986 GT w/T-TOPS<BR>http://www.fiero.nl/cgi-bin/fiero/ubbmisc.cgi||||reg||6
