Z||000017||86SE||09-16-2000||06:10 PM||||Rod, how much did the frame weigh with nothing on it? Just curious......<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero<BR>Special Rally Heavy Duty Suspention||||reg||5
Z||000018||Rodrv6||09-16-2000||11:25 PM||||86, I'm not really sure how much it weighed. I do know that I could pick up either end without too much trouble, and was able to roll it up onto its side by myself.  I must confess that I did leave a couple of things installed.  I didn't remove the rear window or the decklid hinges, but everything else was taken off-even the brake lines and wiring and such.  If I had to guess, I'd say 400 to 500 pounds, but I really don't know.  The car is back togethor and running great-everyone should take one apart and reassemble it.  Great way to learn your car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||1
